居住生活的令人大开眼界的线索</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:07:59 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-3000-year-old-warhorse-burial-and-a-ramses-ii-tablet-among-other-relics-have-been-discovered-in-an-ancient-egyptian-fortress-180989564/</guid></item><item><title>为什么克劳德·莫奈一遍又一遍地画同样的场景？这位印象派艺术家痴迷于捕捉时间的转瞬即逝的本质</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-did-claude-monet-paint-the-same-scenes-over-and-over-again-the-impressionist-artist-was-obsessed-with-capturing-the-fleeting-nature-of-time-180989563/</link><description>泰特现代美术馆即将举办的展览将展出莫奈在 1870 年代至 1920 年代创作的 60 多件艺术作品。这些作品揭示了他如何记录不断变化的光线和天气条件</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:01:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-did-claude-monet-paint-the-same-scenes-over-and-over-again-the-impressionist-artist-was-obsessed-with-capturing-the-fleeting-nature-of-time-180989563/</guid></item><item><title>科学家表示，“超级”厄尔尼诺现象带来的酷热天气可能会在二月份导致近50万人死亡</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-say-scorching-temperatures-brought-on-by-the-super-el-nino-could-kill-nearly-half-a-million-people-by-february-180989555/</link><description>预测数字包括六月以来的死亡人数，可能低估了总死亡人数。炎热天气可能会持续到二月之后，气候变化可能会带来其他危及生命的情况，包括洪水、野火和传染病</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-say-scorching-temperatures-brought-on-by-the-super-el-nino-could-kill-nearly-half-a-million-people-by-february-180989555/</guid></item><item><title>一位金属探测器在德国勘探时惊讶地发现了大量罗马硬币</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-metal-detectorist-exploring-a-field-in-germany-was-stunned-to-discover-a-massive-hoard-of-roman-coins-180989561/</link><description>943 枚第纳尔银币跨越了从公元前 148 年到公元 124 或 125 年近 300 年的罗马历史</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-metal-detectorist-exploring-a-field-in-germany-was-stunned-to-discover-a-massive-hoard-of-roman-coins-180989561/</guid></item><item><title>这幅来源神秘的立体派绘画在芝加哥艺术博物馆悬挂了数十年。现在，博物馆将把它归还给合法的犹太继承人</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-cubist-painting-with-a-mysterious-provenance-hung-in-the-art-institute-of-chicago-for-decades-now-the-museum-will-return-it-to-its-rightful-jewish-heirs-180989553/</link><description>红外成像将 20 世纪 Jean Metzinger 的作品与一位收藏家联系起来，该收藏家的作品在二战期间被纳粹命令强制拍卖</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:18:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-cubist-painting-with-a-mysterious-provenance-hung-in-the-art-institute-of-chicago-for-decades-now-the-museum-will-return-it-to-its-rightful-jewish-heirs-180989553/</guid></item><item><title>土耳其研究人员出土了一块刻有世界上最古老和平条约的古代碎片</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-in-turkey-have-unearthed-an-ancient-fragment-inscribed-with-the-worlds-oldest-peace-treaty-180989554/</link><description>这块泥板刻有阿卡德楔形文字，其文字属于古埃及人和赫梯人于公元前 13 世纪签订的《卡迭石和平条约》</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:39:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-in-turkey-have-unearthed-an-ancient-fragment-inscribed-with-the-worlds-oldest-peace-treaty-180989554/</guid></item><item><title>一只水獭百年来首次回到纽约市布朗克斯河。现在，您可以帮忙命名</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-otter-just-returned-to-new-york-citys-bronx-river-for-the-first-time-in-a-century-now-you-can-help-name-it-180989556/</link><description>今年夏天早些时候，一台追踪相机拍摄了这只动物，这提供了一个充满希望的迹象，表明经过数十年的修复工作，曾经被污染的城市水道正在恢复</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:06:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-otter-just-returned-to-new-york-citys-bronx-river-for-the-first-time-in-a-century-now-you-can-help-name-it-180989556/</guid></item><item><title>科学表明，从促进心理健康到降低痴呆风险，这就是为什么阅读对你非常有益</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-boosting-mental-health-to-reducing-dementia-risk-heres-why-reading-is-extremely-good-for-you-according-to-science-180989548/</link><description>越来越多的证据表明，经常读书可以改善大脑和心理健康，提高读写能力和数学技能，甚至可以减缓认知能力下降。更重要的是，小说似乎还有一个额外的好处，那就是向读者介绍他人的观点</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:33:51 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-boosting-mental-health-to-reducing-dementia-risk-heres-why-reading-is-extremely-good-for-you-according-to-science-180989548/</guid></item><item><title>来认识一下澳大利亚的海豚“泡泡”吧，它会追赶鱼直到它们吐出来，然后吃掉它们吐出来的食物</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-bubbles-a-dolphin-in-australia-that-chases-fish-until-they-barf-then-eats-their-upchucked-meals-180989547/</link><description>科学家记录了 11 次 Bubbles 成功以这种方式吃零食的例子。它们标志着对鲸目动物盗窃食物行为的一些首次详细观察，鲸目动物是海洋哺乳动物，包括海豚、鲸鱼和鼠海豚</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-bubbles-a-dolphin-in-australia-that-chases-fish-until-they-barf-then-eats-their-upchucked-meals-180989547/</guid></item><item><title>通过年度鸟类摄影师大赛的 11 张获奖照片体验鸟类的奇妙</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/experience-the-wonder-of-birds-with-these-11-winning-photos-from-the-bird-photographer-of-the-year-contest-180989552/</link><description>从表演交配表演的大鼠尾草到做鬼脸的黄褐色蛙口，这些照片捕捉到了世界鸟类物种令人惊叹的多样性</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:22:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/experience-the-wonder-of-birds-with-these-11-winning-photos-from-the-bird-photographer-of-the-year-contest-180989552/</guid></item><item><title>这位生活在 14 世纪中国的妇女可能因盗窃或通奸而被割掉鼻子</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-woman-who-lived-in-imperial-china-may-have-had-her-nose-cut-off-as-punishment-for-theft-or-adultery-180989551/</link><description>研究人员在她 700 年前的头骨上发现了愈合的迹象，这表明她在痛苦的制裁中幸存下来，甚至可能继续佩戴假肢</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:30:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-woman-who-lived-in-imperial-china-may-have-had-her-nose-cut-off-as-punishment-for-theft-or-adultery-180989551/</guid></item></channel></rss>